(Guidance on Risk-Weighted Assets Calculation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(Risk-weighted assets \(RWA\) form the denominator in capital adequacy ratios and are a key) Tj
T*
(component of the Basel regulatory framework. This document outlines the methodologies) Tj
T*
(for calculating RWA for credit risk, market risk, and operational risk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Credit Risk RWA) Tj
T*
(2.1 Standardized Approach) Tj
T*
(Under the standardized approach, banks assign risk weights to assets based on external) Tj
T*
(credit assessments or prescribed regulatory risk weights.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.1.1 Sovereign Exposures) Tj
T*
(- AAA to AA-: 0%) Tj
T*
(- A+ to A-: 20%) Tj
T*
(- BBB+ to BBB-: 50%) Tj
T*
(- BB+ to B-: 100%) Tj
T*
(- Below B-: 150%) Tj
T*
(- Unrated: 100%) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.1.2 Bank Exposures) Tj
T*
(- Option 1: Risk weight based on sovereign rating of country of incorporation) Tj
T*
(- Option 2: Risk weight based on external credit assessment of bank) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.1.3 Corporate Exposures) Tj
T*
(- AAA to AA-: 20%) Tj
T*
(- A+ to A-: 50%) Tj
T*
(- BBB+ to BB-: 100%) Tj
T*
(- Below BB-: 150%) Tj
T*
(- Unrated: 100%) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.2 Foundation Internal Ratings-Based \(F-IRB\) Approach) Tj
T*
(Banks using the F-IRB approach estimate the probability of default \(PD\) for each) Tj
T*
(exposure, while the regulator provides other risk parameters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.3 Advanced Internal Ratings-Based \(A-IRB\) Approach) Tj
T*
(Banks using the A-IRB approach estimate all risk parameters: PD, loss given default) Tj
T*
(\(LGD\), exposure at default \(EAD\), and effective maturity \(M\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Market Risk RWA) Tj
T*
(3.1 Standardized Approach for Market Risk) Tj
T*
(The standardized approach uses prescribed risk weights for interest rate risk, equity) Tj
T*
(risk, foreign exchange risk, commodity risk, and credit spread risk.) Tj
