(8.1 Regulatory Reporting) Tj
T*
(Banks must report RWA calculations to regulators on a quarterly basis, including) Tj
T*
(breakdowns by risk type and approach.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(8.2 Public Disclosure) Tj
T*
(Banks must publicly disclose RWA amounts and key risk parameters as part of Pillar 3) Tj
T*
(requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Validation and Review) Tj
T*
(9.1 Model Validation) Tj
T*
(Banks using internal models must establish comprehensive validation frameworks,) Tj
T*
(including back-testing and stress testing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9.2 Supervisory Review) Tj
T*
(Regulators review RWA calculations and models as part of the supervisory review process) Tj
T*
(\(Pillar 2\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Recent Developments) Tj
T*
(10.1 Basel III Revisions) Tj
T*
(Recent Basel III revisions aim to reduce excessive variability in RWA calculations and) Tj
T*
(improve comparability across banks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10.2 Output Floor) Tj
T*
(The output floor limits the extent to which banks can use internal models to reduce RWA) Tj
T*
(relative to the standardized approach.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Implementation Challenges) Tj
T*
(11.1 Data Requirements) Tj
T*
(RWA calculations require comprehensive data on exposures, collateral, and risk) Tj
T*
(parameters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11.2 System Integration) Tj
T*
(Banks must integrate RWA calculation systems with risk management, finance, and) Tj
T*
(regulatory reporting systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. Conclusion) Tj
T*
(Accurate calculation of risk-weighted assets is essential for determining capital) Tj
T*
(adequacy and ensuring the resilience of the banking system. Banks must maintain robust) Tj
T*
(methodologies, systems, and controls for RWA calculation and reporting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Financial Stability Board) Tj
T*
(Basel Committee on Banking Supervision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
